Measured before the code: every preview answer was the whole identity body with
no Content-Encoding and no Vary, so a client naming gzip still paid 55185B for
preview/index.html and an intermediate cache could not tell the two
representations apart; If-Match and If-Unmodified-Since were dropped entirely,
so a reader could not demand "only if this is still the version I hold".
Landed: _accepts_gzip (explicit token beats the wildcard, q=0 refuses, an
unreadable q falls back to the token default), Handler._negotiate (gzip only
for a whole-body answer of at least 64 bytes; a range always addresses the
identity bytes), Handler._precondition_failed (If-Match strong comparison first,
If-Unmodified-Since only when If-Match is absent), Vary: Accept-Encoding on
every reply, 412 with a named body, and gzip negotiation on the root page too.
